    <string name="set_privacy">Your dreams stay on this phone: no account, no internet, no tracking. Speaking a dream uses your phone’s own speech recognition.</string>
    <string name="set_credit">The look is a tribute to Winsor McCay’s Little Nemo in Slumberland (1905–1914). Every picture is drawn by the app itself.</string>

    <!-- Welcome -->
    <string name="w1_title">A dream becomes a page</string>
    <string name="w1_text">Tell the app what you dreamt, in a few words or many. It cuts the story into panels and draws each one: where you were, who was there, what happened, how it felt. Your words go underneath.</string>
    <string name="w2_title">Your own dreamland</string>
    <string name="w2_text">Places and people come back. Name them once and they appear on your atlas and in your cast. Nemo’s bed grows legs as you remember more mornings and walks out across the map.</string>
    <string name="w3_title">Catch it on waking</string>
    <string name="w3_text">A dream fades in minutes. Around the time you wake, a quiet note; the screen opens dark and dim so you can tell it half asleep.</string>

